#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
apply-nodalis-v5-fixes.py

===============================================================================
 HOW TO USE THIS
===============================================================================

 1. Put this file in the same folder as your index.html.
 2. Open a terminal in that folder.
 3. Run:

        python3 apply-nodalis-v5-fixes.py index.html

    On Windows, if `python3` is not found, use:

        py apply-nodalis-v5-fixes.py index.html

 4. It prints one line per change and finishes with a summary.
    Your original is saved next to it as index.html.bak

 That is all. No installing anything, no build step. Python 3.6 or newer.

 IF SOMETHING IS WRONG it writes NOTHING and tells you why:
   * "already applied"  - you have run it before. Nothing changed.
   * "does not look like the right index.html" - it needs the file that came
     out of apply-nodalis-v4-fixes.py. Send me the file you have and I will
     rebuild the patch for it.
   * a list of edits that did not match - the file was hand-edited since.

 TO UNDO: delete index.html and rename index.html.bak back to index.html.

===============================================================================
 WHAT IT CHANGES
===============================================================================

 FOUR BUGS YOU REPORTED
   * a menu tall enough to scroll closed itself the moment you scrolled it
   * mobile sheet rows could not grow, so long labels printed over each other
     (the jumbled "Vault tools" list)
   * Trash and "Check my vault" were unreachable outside a phone, because the
     More button was hidden on wider screens
   * the note "..." button was too faint to see in some themes

 TEN FEATURES
   1. Share a note as a real FILE through your phone's share sheet
   2. Publish a note as a link that updates when you publish again
   3. Share a folder, a selection, or the whole vault as a zip
   4. Copy with formatting, for pasting into Gmail, Word or Docs
   5. Note icons
   6. Note colours
   7. Lock a note so it cannot be edited by accident
   8. A word goal per note, with progress in the bottom bar
   9. Reopen the last closed note - Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+T
  10. Select several notes in the sidebar and move, tag, export or delete them

 New keys, all chosen to avoid the ones already in use:
   Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+Shift+S   share this note
   Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+L         lock / unlock
   Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+M         the More menu
   Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+Shift+T   reopen the last closed note
"""
import io
import os
import shutil
import sys

